<title>USA: SanDisk sets shareholder rights plan.</title>
<headline>SanDisk sets shareholder rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>SanDisk Corp said it set a shareholder rights plan that will be triggered if a third party seeks to buy or buys 15 percent of the company.</p>
<p>The plan permits Seagate Technology Inc to continue to hold its 25 percent stake in the company, SanDisk said.</p>
<p>SanDisk officials were not immediately available to comment on the action.</p>
<p>The plan grants one preferred share purchase right on each outstanding share of SanDisk's common stock.</p>
